    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (85.72), who remains our strongest play despite a 37% rain risk. Facing Ryan Feltner, **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a 14% park factor advantage. **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) and **Andy Pages** (75.64) are our next most vital assets; **Luis Robert Jr.** is ideally positioned for a breakout against Ray, leveraging a 14% platoon edge, while **Andy Pages**\u2014also tied to the Feltner matchup\u2014benefits significantly from favorable park conditions. We are also leaning heavily into the power-speed combination of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), whose 16% park boost against Baz makes him a primary offensive engine for the day.\n\nStrategy today heavily weights the stolen base premium, leading to the deployment of **Nasim Nunez** (61.74) and **Heliot Ramos** (70.20). **Nasim Nunez** is a specific target against the slow delivery of Quantrill, providing elite speed utility despite a lower lineup placement. Conversely, the most difficult benching decision involved **Jackson Merrill** (55.05); while his raw projections were respectable, he was ultimately squeezed out by the efficiency of **Wade Meckler** (59.97) and **Sam Antonacci** (57.41) in favorable platoon spots. **Jackson Merrill** suffered from an unfavorable matchup against Thornton, forcing us to prioritize the higher situational scores of our daily starters. \n\nWhile we are optimized for maximum efficiency, monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** closely due to the aforementioned rain risk in their venue. We remain without **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** due to his ongoing IL stint, and while we have bench depth in **Miguel Vargas** and **Luis Lara**, their current projected output falls below the threshold required to displace our primary starters. **Drake Baldwin** (64.82) provides a surprisingly high floor from the leadoff spot, and provided **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** navigate the tough matchup against Rod\u00f3n, we are well-positioned to maintain our lead in the 5x5 standings.",
